  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pakistan Acute Crisis Joint Response (PKJR)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pakistan has been enduring severe monsoon weather since June 2022, which saw area weighted rainfall 67 per cent above normal levels in that month alone. As of August 27, rainfall in the country is equivalent to 2.9 times the national 30-year average. This has caused widespread flooding and landslides, with severe repercussions for human lives, property and infrastructure. 
The objective of the JR is to provide flood-affected people with lifesaving humanitarian assistance. 

Tearfund will provide farming input packages, consisting of wheat seed and fertilizer (sufficient for harvesting 1 acre per family) to 800 HH in Sindh and 650 HH in Punjab and Two rounds of unconditional and unrestricted cash distributions (PKR 25.000 per HH per round), In Sindh 335 HH, in Punjab 430HH</narrative>
  </description>
